MID_SE_Ism_Sar_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Ism_Sar_A_001: Promised One? You asked to see me?
MID_SE_Ism_Sar_A_002: Oh! This is your favored spear, isn't it?
MID_SE_Ism_Sar_A_003: I don't understand. Why are you offering it to me?
MID_SE_Ism_Sar_A_004: <NCA>"I want you to feel safe."
MID_SE_Ism_Sar_A_005: Is it that obvious?
MID_SE_Ism_Sar_A_006: It's true, and you know it, so I'll just be honest.\nI don't fully trust you, Promised One.
MID_SE_Ism_Sar_A_007: Everyone admires you. Those who fight beside you,\nof course, but also everyone else we meet.
MID_SE_Ism_Sar_A_008: It's a good story. A brave hero suddenly appears,\nready to slay the evil god Balor.
MID_SE_Ism_Sar_A_009: With the world looking like it's ending, you bring\nthe hope we need. 
MID_SE_Ism_Sar_A_010: That feels a bit too...convenient.
MID_SE_Ism_Sar_A_011: <NCA>"..."
MID_SE_Ism_Sar_A_012: <NCB>"Isn't that what Mediators do too?"
MID_SE_Ism_Sar_A_013: <ACA>You're always so quiet, but I need you to talk to\nme right now.
MID_SE_Ism_Sar_A_014: <ACA>I'm from the village of Kunlun. I know you're\na Mediator. 
MID_SE_Ism_Sar_A_015: <ACB>That's true. I suppose. In a way.
MID_SE_Ism_Sar_A_016: <ACB>A Mediator is created when people need their help.
MID_SE_Ism_Sar_A_017: <ACB>And I know that you were made as a Mediator.
MID_SE_Ism_Sar_A_018: But there's something different about you.
MID_SE_Ism_Sar_A_019: I spent time with Anatolia and Nezha just after they\nwere created.
MID_SE_Ism_Sar_A_020: And I've seen other Mediators, so I think I know\na fair bit about them.
MID_SE_Ism_Sar_A_021: Still, when I look at you, and at them...you're, well,\nyou're different. But I can't quite tell you why.
MID_SE_Ism_Sar_A_022: Mm...
MID_SE_Ism_Sar_A_023: You showed up and risked your own life without any\nhesitation at all.
MID_SE_Ism_Sar_A_024: I'm not saying that's bad, not really. But it does\nfeel—I don't know—almost inhuman?
MID_SE_Ism_Sar_A_025: Even Anatolia had some moments of hesitation\nwhen she started out.
MID_SE_Ism_Sar_A_026: That's why I doubted you. I even thought about\ntrying to look into your background.
MID_SE_Ism_Sar_A_027: <NCA>"I understand."
MID_SE_Ism_Sar_A_028: <NCB>"I don't mind."
MID_SE_Ism_Sar_A_029: Really? Even after everything I've said, you're\nstill unfazed?
MID_SE_Ism_Sar_A_030: I think I do want to look into your past. If there's\nnothing amiss, I will give you back your spear.
MID_SE_Ism_Sar_A_031: <NCA>"Are you sure?"
MID_SE_Ism_Sar_A_032: It's not like I think you're my enemy.
MID_SE_Ism_Sar_A_033: But, since I have your permission, I'm going to\nfind out everything I can about you.
MID_SE_Ism_Sar_S: <EDH>
MID_SE_Ism_Sar_S_001: I never thought I'd come here. I've always hated\ngoing to temples.
MID_SE_Ism_Sar_S_002: I really don't want to pray, but...
MID_SE_Ism_Sar_S_003: Promised One! You're alive?
MID_SE_Ism_Sar_S_004: I know healing magic! If you're hurt, I can help.
MID_SE_Ism_Sar_S_005: <NCA>"I'm fine."
MID_SE_Ism_Sar_S_006: You are? Really? That's good.
MID_SE_Ism_Sar_S_007: I'm happy I get to talk to you like this again.
MID_SE_Ism_Sar_S_008: I want to apologize. Do you remember when I said I\ndoubted you, and I was going to look into your past?
MID_SE_Ism_Sar_S_009: <NCA>"It doesn't matter."
MID_SE_Ism_Sar_S_010: <NCB>"Honestly, I'd forgotten."
MID_SE_Ism_Sar_S_011: <ACA>You don't care? I guess that's typical of you.
MID_SE_Ism_Sar_S_012: <ACB>You did? Well, that's a little disappointing.
MID_SE_Ism_Sar_S_013: I did look into it. I learned all I could.
MID_SE_Ism_Sar_S_014: And what I found was that you're a very\nspecial person.
MID_SE_Ism_Sar_S_015: You are quiet and mysterious, and so kind.
MID_SE_Ism_Sar_S_016: I finally understood that everything you do is to\nmake everyone else happy and safe.
MID_SE_Ism_Sar_S_017: Like everyone else, I've begun to admire you.\nI mean that. I do.
MID_SE_Ism_Sar_S_018: Although, you're probably going to say I should have\nseen you were good without having to look into it.
MID_SE_Ism_Sar_S_019: <NCA>"I'd like to know you better too."
MID_SE_Ism_Sar_S_020: You want to know about me?
MID_SE_Ism_Sar_S_021: I mean, I can't be that interesting. I've never done\nmuch worth talking about.
MID_SE_Ism_Sar_S_022: But, I think I would like you to know me.\nEverything there is to share.
MID_SE_Ism_Sar_S_023: <RSDS>I'm not going to just blurt it all out though. I studied\nyou—now you have to do the same for me.
MID_SE_Ism_Sar_S_024: I will tell you one secret though. I like it when you\npay attention to me.